	<skos:broader rdf:resource="http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L06/current/48"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The East Australian Current 4700m Mooring is operated by CSIRO Oceans and Atmosphere, and collects data in the East Australian Current. This mooring forms part of the second deployment of the EAC array, and was reconfigured to incorporate parts of the continental shelf. The array that this mooring was part of was decommissioned in July 2022.</skos:definition>
